Hint:\(W = \overrightarrow{F}\cdot \overrightarrow{s}\)

Step:Find the work done on the body during time interval\(t= 2~\text{s
and}~3~\text{s}.\)
The displacement of the particle is given by;
\(x(t)=\alpha t^2+\beta t+\gamma m\)
After putting values of\(\alpha, \beta, \gamma\)in above equation we get;
\( x(t)=t^2+t+1\)
The velocity of the particle is given by;
\(v(t)=\dfrac{dx}{dt}=2 t+1\)
The initial velocity of the particle (at \(t= 2~\text{s}\)) is given by;
\(v_i = 5~\text{m/s}\)
The final velocity of the particle (at \(t= 3~\text{s}\)) is given by;
\(v_f= 7~\text{m/s}\)
According the work energy theorem, the work done on the body is given by;
\(W = \dfrac{1}{2}m\left(v^2_f- v^2_i\right)= \dfrac{1}{2}\times 2\times
(49-25)= 24~\text{J}\)
Hence, option (3) is the correct answer.<div style="margin-top:1.25rem; padding:0.85rem 1rem; background:var(--bg-secondary); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px;"><div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:0.6rem; font-weight:600; font-size:0.88rem;"><span>📊 Student Attempt Analytics</span><span style="padding:2px 8px; border-radius:12px; font-size:0.75rem; font-weight:700; background:rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.15); color:#16a34a;">🟢 Easy · 86% Got This Correct</span></div><div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0.5rem; text-align:center; font-size:0.82rem;"><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(1)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">3%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(2)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">7%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:rgba(34,197,94,0.12); border:1.5px solid #22c55e;"><div style="color:#16a34a; font-weight:700;">(3) ✓</div><div style="font-weight:800; color:#16a34a; margin-top:2px;">87%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(4)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">6%</div></div></div></div>

